      "description": "After twelve years of Jineolojî work in Europe, the Kurdish women’s science is undergoing a reorientation. Existing methods are to be reviewed, research projects more closely linked to everyday social life, and new forms of communal organization developed. Kira Legerhausen of the Jineolojî Academy spoke to ANF about these issues on the sidelines of the European Jineolojî Conference in Haelen, the Netherlands. Her focus is on women’s living conditions, overcoming patriarchal relationships, and exploring how scientific knowledge can contribute to tangible social change. “We have entered an important phase. It is a process of rebuilding, change, and transformation,” Legerhausen explained. Over ",
